      en: "The Governmental Palace of Oyem is the seat of the Woleu-Ntem provincial administration. Built in the 1970s, it blends modern architecture with traditional elements. It houses the governor's office and administrative staff. Located in the center of Oyem, it is surrounded by a large garden. Nearby are the prefecture and other government buildings. The palace symbolizes state authority in northern Gabon.",
